:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}3\\,\\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}f(x,y,g(x,y))\\sqrt{1+{(\\frac{∂z}{∂x})}^{2}+{(\\frac{∂z}{∂y})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A\\\\ & ={∬}_{D}3\\sqrt{1+\\left(2\\right)^{2}+\\left(2\\right)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A\\\\ & ={∬}_{D}9\\,\\text{d}A\\\\ & =9{∬}_{D}\\,\\text{d}A\\\\ & =9\\cdot\\text{Area}(D)\\\\ & =9\\cdot\\left(2-\\left(1\\right)\\right)\\cdot\\left(2-\\left(0\\right)\\right)\\\\ & =9\\cdot\\left(1\\right)\\cdot\\left(2\\right)\\\\ & =18.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535961 17592186045443 true] [17592186549197 1080 "6" 13194139535961 17592186045443 true] [17592186549197 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139535961 17592186045443 true] [17592186549197 1083 #uuid "1071da23-196f-5794-9ffa-3f740ac06877" 13194139535961 17592186045443 true] [17592186549198 1068 #edb/ref 17592186549225 13194139535961 17592186045443 true] [17592186549198 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139535961 17592186045443 true] [17592186549198 1071 "Evaluate the surface integral\n\n$$\n\\iint_S \\frac{4}{\\sqrt{z-x+y^{2}}}\\,\\mathrm{d}S\n$$\n\nwhere $S$ is defined by $z=x + y^{2} + 1$ for $1\\le x\\le 2$ and $-2\\le y\\le 2$." 13194139535961 17592186045443 true] [17592186549198 1072 #uuid "161eeef3-7763-576b-af4d-53c8662ff260" 13194139535961 17592186045443 true] [17592186549198 1074 "For a surface $S$ defined by $z=g(x,y)$ with $(x,y)\\in D,$ the surface integral of a scalar function $f(x,y,z)$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}f(x,y,g(x,y))\\sqrt{1+{(\\frac{∂z}{∂x})}^{2}+{(\\frac{∂z}{∂y})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nFor the partial derivatives, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂z}{∂x}=\\frac{∂}{∂x}(x + y^{2} + 1)=1,\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂z}{∂y}=\\frac{∂}{∂y}(x + y^{2} + 1)=2 y.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral can be evaluated as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{z-x+y^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}f(x,y,g(x,y))\\sqrt{1+{(\\frac{∂z}{∂x})}^{2}+{(\\frac{∂z}{∂y})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A\\\\ & ={∬}_{D}\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{\\left(x + y^{2} + 1\\right)-